  "keySyntax": {
    "modifiers": [
      "ctrl",
      "shift",
      "alt",
      "cmd"
    ],
    "aliases": {
      "control": "ctrl",
      "opt": "alt",
      "option": "alt",
      "meta": "alt",
      "command": "cmd",
      "super": "cmd",
      "win": "cmd",
      "esc": "escape",
      "return": "enter"
    },
    "specialKeys": [
      "escape",
      "enter",
      "tab",
      "space",
      "up",
      "down",
      "left",
      "right",
      "pageup",
      "pagedown",
      "home",
      "end",
      "backspace",
      "delete",
      "wheelup",
      "wheeldown"
    ],
    "chordSeparator": " ",
    "notes": [
      "The file is ~/.claude/keybindings.json. The /keybindings command in Claude Code creates or opens it.",
      "The top level is an object. It may hold $schema and $docs, and it holds a bindings array of blocks.",
      "A block has a context name and a bindings object. Each key string in that object maps to an action id or to null.",
      "Claude Code picks up edits to the file on its own. No restart is needed.",
      "Key names ignore case, so K and k are the same. Write shift+k to mean Shift with a letter.",
      "Join modifiers and the key with +, as in ctrl+shift+c.",
      "A chord is several keystrokes separated by a space, as in ctrl+k ctrl+s. Each press must come within 3 seconds of the last.",
      "The cmd group only works in terminals that report the Super key, such as those with the Kitty keyboard protocol or xterm modifyOtherKeys. Most terminals do not, so ctrl or meta is safer.",
      "alt, opt, option and meta all mean Alt on Windows and Linux and Option on macOS.",
      "Setting an action to null removes a default binding. This works for chords too. Remove every chord that shares a prefix to use that prefix as a single key.",
      "If only some chords on a prefix are removed, the prefix still waits for a second keystroke.",
      "Claude Code reads a misspelled modifier such as ctl+k as plain k. It only logs a warning, which you see when you start with --debug.",
      "An unknown action name is skipped, and the default binding for that key stays.",
      "A bare letter, digit or space that you bind still types normally inside dialog text fields.",
      "Write Ctrl shortcuts with Latin letters, whatever the keyboard layout.",
      "The docs do not mention function keys such as f1, so support is unknown.",
      "Pane and PaneField belong to mods. The docs give default chords for them but no action names.",
      "MessageSelector has no actions of its own. It uses the Select actions.",
      "Default chords that start with ctrl+x: Chat has ctrl+x ctrl+k, ctrl+x ctrl+e, ctrl+x enter, ctrl+x ctrl+a, ctrl+x ctrl+s and ctrl+x tab. Task has ctrl+x ctrl+b. DiffPanel has ctrl+x b. Pane has ctrl+x left, right, up, down and x. PaneField has ctrl+x x.",
      "The docs name no context for the history actions, so they list none."
    ]
  },
  "reservedKeys": [
    {
      "key": "ctrl+c",
      "reason": "Fixed to interrupt"
    },
    {
      "key": "ctrl+d",
      "reason": "Fixed to exit"
    },
    {
      "key": "ctrl+m",
      "reason": "Arrives as Enter"
    },
    {
      "key": "ctrl+[",
      "reason": "Arrives as Escape. With the Kitty keyboard protocol this needs v2.1.242 or later"
    },
    {
      "key": "ctrl+i",
      "reason": "Arrives as Tab"
    },
    {
      "key": "ctrl+h",
      "reason": "Sends the backspace byte. How it reads depends on the terminal"
    },
